@startuml Sequence Diagram - Network Error
title Escenario 3 - Error de Red (Simulator API)
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam ArrowColor #666666
skinparam LifeLineBorderColor #666666

participant "Comercio\n(Backend)" as Comercio
participant "SDK KitPagos" as SDK
participant "Simulator API\n(Fastify)" as SimAPI
participant "Scenario Engine" as Engine

Comercio -> SDK : createPayment(CreatePaymentRequest)
SDK -> SimAPI : POST /simulate/{gateway}/payments
SimAPI -> Engine : resolveScenario(orderReference) -> "network_error"

alt Timeout (SDK no responde dentro del umbral)
  Engine -->x SDK : sin respuesta\n(latencia inyectada > timeout)
  SDK -->x SDK : socket hang up / AbortError
  SDK -> SDK : mapear a SdkError(GATEWAY_TIMEOUT\no CONNECTION_FAILED)
else Error de servidor simulado
  Engine --> SimAPI : 5xx (Wompi/MP/Rapyd) o 200 con\ncode="ERROR" (Kushki)
  SimAPI --> SDK : respuesta de error nativa
  SDK -> SDK : mapear codigo HTTP o body.code\n-> SdkErrorCode
end

SDK -->x Comercio : throw SdkError{code, friendlyMessage,\ngateway, httpStatus, originalError}

note bottom
  Kushki SIEMPRE devuelve HTTP 200: el adaptador debe leer
  body.code/body.error, NO el status HTTP, para decidir
  GATEWAY_SERVER_ERROR. Rapyd SI usa codigos HTTP
  diferenciados (200/400/401), a diferencia de PayU/Kushki
  (docs.rapyd.net/en/list-payments.html) — leer tambien
  body.status.error_code para el detalle.
end note

@enduml
